-- title:
--   Irreducibility of the π₀-fibre of the j-finite chart
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$, in the sense that the image of $q$ lies in $A.\mathrm{nonunits}$. Let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ an element whose image lies in $A$, and write $A_0$ for the valuation subring $A$ pulled back along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$; assume $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$, and that every $a \in A$ is congruent, modulo the maximal ideal of $A$, to some $c \in k_0$ with $c \in A$. Let $N \ge 1$ with $q \nmid N$, let $H \le (\mathbb Z/N)^\times$, and let $K''$ be an intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,k_0$ over $k_0$ equal to the $k_0$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the function field $\mathrm{xHFunctionField}\,N\,H$ of $X_H(N)$ over $\mathbb Q$, regarded as an $A_0$-algebra compatibly with $A_0 \to k_0 \to K''$. Let $j'' \in K''$ be nonzero with underlying Laurent series the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion $\mathrm{jq}$ of $j$. Then, inside the $A_0$-subalgebra $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_0\,K''\,j''$ of $K''$ (the $j$-finite chart of the two-chart integral model, namely $\mathrm{chartAlg}\,A_0\,K''\,\{j''\}$), every minimal prime $P$ over the ideal generated by the image of $\pi_0$ is contained in every prime ideal $\mathfrak y$ of that subalgebra which contains the image of $\pi_0$.
--
--   This is the chart-side form of good reduction of $X_H(N)$ at a prime $q$ not dividing $N$: the special fibre of the $j$-finite chart of the two-chart integral model over $A_0$ has a unique irreducible component, stated as the assertion that the minimal primes over $\pi_0$ are minimal among all primes containing $\pi_0$. It is used in the analysis of the reduction of the full-level modular curve, through [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.mem_of_coe_mem_nonunits_of_isMaximal_of_mem_ssJSet_chartAlgFin`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.mem_of_coe_mem_nonunits_of_isMaximal_of_mem_ssJSet_chartAlgFin).
